# Security

- Never commit `.env`, tokens, PATs, API keys, SQLite files, uploads, or exports
- Jira/ADO/OpenAI secrets are server-side only; mask after save in UI
- Do not log credentials, raw Authorization headers, or full transcripts to insecure sinks
- Least-privilege read scopes for Jira and Azure DevOps
- Unpublished assessments and admin APIs require authorization
- Treat workshop transcripts and remote contributions as sensitive data
- Use platform secret injection on Railway and OpenShift
